NAME
     tr - translate or delete characters

SYNOPSIS
     tr [-d] [-s] [-c] SET1 [SET2]

DESCRIPTION
     tr copies standard input to standard output, replacing each
     character of SET1 with the one in the same position of SET2. The
     sets may use ranges (a-z), and the escapes \n, \t and \\, and the
     classes [:alpha:], [:digit:], [:space:], [:upper:] and [:lower:].

OPTIONS
     -d   delete the characters of SET1 instead of replacing them
     -s   squeeze runs of the same character into one
     -c   use the complement of SET1

SEE ALSO
     sed(1), cut(1)
